e a 100 MiB hard limit for `datauser` on the filesystem backing `/srv/data`. The mandatory restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures healthy pre-restart quota/data state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID, recovered quota and data state, and successful post-restart enforcement. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The quota is a per-user quota on the root filesystem backing `/srv/data`, so it also counts any files `datauser` can create elsewhere on that filesystem; the evidence does not demonstrate directory-exclusive accounting.","Lifecycle failed-service collection is unsupported on this Alpine node, although the relevant OpenRC `local` service was directly observed as started after reboot.","Final existence of `/etc/fstab.pre-datauser-quota` was not directly listed; its retention is inferred from its creation and the absence of any cleanup command in the complete timeline."]}
